# homelab#1705: `-32602` is goose's CODE — the class NAME in content is text (goose row), and a
# claude ride cannot die of it even in the real shape (claude row); neither is harness-death.
rawlog-32602-content-echo-goose |       |       |     | rawlog-32602-content-echo-goose |
rawlog-32602-claude-harness     |       |       |     | rawlog-32602-claude-harness     |
# Retro r8 F3 (docs/agents/retros/2026-10-12-platform-r8-opus.md): the two cap signatures that used
# to file as a deliberate stop. The forced-final-output pair is goose-gated and matched as a PAIR
# (the phrase alone is content — #1705); goose's 402 line is owner-ambiguous, hence the residual arm.
rawlog-output-token-cap               |       |       |     | rawlog-output-token-cap               |
rawlog-output-token-cap-with-pr       |       |       |     | rawlog-output-token-cap-with-pr       |
rawlog-output-token-content-echo      |       |       |     | rawlog-output-token-content-echo      |
rawlog-output-token-cap-claude-harness |       |       |     | rawlog-output-token-cap-claude-harness |
