stats-turn-cap                        |       |       |     | stats-turn-cap                        |
# FU-270 / homelab#2867 (operator ruling 2026-10-24): opencode auto-rejected its own permission —
# `harness-fault` (gateway scope harness), in BOTH branches; the pair quoted in content (indented)
# is text, and the pair is opencode's, so another harness's log never matches it.
stats-harness-fault                   |       |       |     | stats-harness-fault                   |
rawlog-harness-fault                  |       |       |     | rawlog-harness-fault                  |
rawlog-harness-fault-content-echo     |       |       |     | rawlog-harness-fault-content-echo     |
rawlog-harness-fault-goose-harness    |       |       |     | rawlog-harness-fault-goose-harness    |
# homelab#3094: an OOMKilled agent container takes agent-finalize with it, so only this fallback
# sees the ride. The kubelet's terminated reason is the evidence (no log signature exists) and it
# outranks the log greps, as DeadlineExceeded does; a PR does not silence it (a death, not a round).
rawlog-oomkilled                      |       |       |     | rawlog-oomkilled                      |
rawlog-oomkilled-with-pr              |       |       |     | rawlog-oomkilled-with-pr              |
rawlog-oomkilled-outranks-log         |       |       |     | rawlog-oomkilled-outranks-log         |
rawlog-agent-error-not-oom            |       |       |     | rawlog-agent-error-not-oom            |
